<title>USA: USDA cuts Brazil 1996 orange juice export forecast.</title>
<headline>USDA cuts Brazil 1996 orange juice export forecast.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department Monday estimated Brazil orange juice exports in 1996 (Brazilian marketing year July 1996-June 1997) at 1.05 million tonnes, down from its previous forecast of 1.08 million tonnes.</p>
<p>USDA said it shaved the forecast based on likely lower exports to the United States due to expected larger U.S. production.  </p>
<p>In its World Horticultural Trade and U.S. Export Opportunities report, USDA said its estimate for Brazil 1995/96 orange juice production (marketed in 1996/97) was unchanged at 1.06 million tonnes.</p>
</text>
